  "split_key_first (design-v2 section 10.2)": "PqxdhDeploymentIdealKeyFirst.split_key_first and split_key_last (material (key32, nonce12) of slot 0 first; the seed stays a world seed)",
  "world_key_first": "dropped (design-v2 section 10.2, S14)"
 },
 "deviations_from_design": [
  "the coupling replaces owner k's secret key in the guesser's state by a key of the guesser's own (swapX), read by no step before the selected raw accept except owner k's finish, which the decapsulation oracle answers under the selected key; the real run keeps the invariant that owner k holds the selected secret key (HoldsX) (implementation-level; consistent with plan section 84, which rejects only decapsulation under another key)",
  "the oracle finish answers every finish of owner k while the selected accept is not active, not only the first one in initSent (finishes outside initSent make no decapsulation request); no stopping time inside the guesser, which runs the whole game; the guess is frozen at the selected raw accept (implementation-level)",
  "the defined quantity is named ctGuessByCca (the brief wrote ctGuessBy, which names the frozen oracle-free form); ctGuessByCca_ambient and ctGuessByCca_le_pk relate them",
  "the guesser outputs an optional ciphertext; the hit event is some of the encapsulation ciphertext",
  "two modules for anomaly_le_pk (PqxdhDeploymentIdealKeySwap registered in this track, PqxdhDeploymentIdealAnomalyGuesser)",
  "the guesser's uniform-query count and zero base-oracle count are not stated as theorems (open for CE-12a if its headline lists the adversary caps)",
  "U8 statements hold for every view erasing the hidden-slot service state; the key-first game runs over the lazy slot cache (lazyService) after idealGame_lazy, because the counted table breaks exact commutation with completions"
 ],
